Comment (internal/authz/cedar.go:178):
**[Medium] Principal/resource entity-UID collision silently drops the principal's roles.**

`principal` is written into `entities` at line 175 carrying the role parents, then `resource` is written here. When both resolve to the **same** Cedar UID, this second write overwrites the principal entity and replaces its role parents with an empty set, so `principal in CCF::Role::"…"` no longer matches and the request is **denied even though the role grants it**.

This happens whenever a principal acts on a resource of its own kind with `resource.ID == subject.ID`: a `user` subject on a `user` resource, or an `agent` subject on an `agent` resource (both `principalUID` and `resourceUID` produce `CCF::User`/`CCF::Agent` for those, since `cedarEntityName("agent") == "Agent"`). It is *not* reachable by the two routes wired today (`evidence:create`, `admin:manage`), but the manifest's `agent` role explicitly grants the `agent` resource (`register`, `ingest`), so it goes live the moment an agent self-route is wired with the agent id as `:id`.

Confirmed empirically: agent `ingest` on the `agent` resource → **allow** with empty id, **allow** with a different id, **deny** when the id equals the agent's own subject id.

The resource id is meant to be irrelevant to a C0 (type-only) decision, which is what makes this so easy to miss. Fix: don't let the resource entity clobber the principal entity — when they share a UID the principal entity already satisfies `resource is CCF::Agent` (same type) while keeping its parents:

```go
if resource != principal {
    entities[resource] = cedar.Entity{UID: resource, Parents: cedar.NewEntityUIDSet()}
}
```

A regression test (agent `ingest` on `Resource{Type:"agent", ID: <subject.ID>}` must allow) would lock it in.
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** Agreed — real bug. Fix in Cedar.decide: guard the resource entity write so it never clobbers the principal entity (which carries the role parents). When principal==resource UID, the principal entity already satisfies `resource is CCF::Agent`/`CCF::User` (same type) while keeping its parents. Adding regression test: agent `ingest` on Resource{Type:"agent", ID:<subject.ID>} must allow.

