Comment (internal/authz/cedar.go:147):
**[Low] Batch role memo ignores `Subject.Props["groups"]`.**

The memo key is `{Subject.Type, Subject.ID}`, but `rolesFor` also depends on the subject's `groups` prop. Two `EvalRequest`s that share a type+id but carry different `groups` would get the first request's roles reused. Harmless for the only current consumer (`/me/permissions` sends one subject repeatedly), and groups are inert until BCH-1328 — but if the batch API is ever fed heterogeneous subjects sharing an id, decisions would be silently wrong. Consider either documenting "batch assumes one logical subject per (type,id)" or folding a hash of the normalized groups into the memo key.
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** Agreed — fold the normalized groups into the batch memo key so heterogeneous subjects sharing a (type,id) can never reuse the wrong roles (correct now rather than a doc caveat that bites when BCH-1328 makes groups live). Key becomes type\x00id\x00sorted-groups.

